msgstr ""

#: src/orcshot/ui/extension_install.py:73
msgid ""
"Orcshot's tray icon, region selection and window picker on Wayland run "
"inside GNOME Shell as an extension. Snap packages aren't allowed to install "
"extensions, so this one comes from GNOME's own extension site.\n"
"\n"
"1. Click Open extensions.gnome.org below.\n"
"2. Search for Orcshot and open its page.\n"
"3. Switch the toggle to ON.\n"
"4. That's it — this window closes by itself when the extension is running.\n"
"\n"
"If the page says your browser needs the GNOME Shell integration add-on: "
"install the add-on it links to, then on Ubuntu run  sudo apt install gnome-"
"browser-connector  (or install Extension Manager from the Software app and "
"search for Orcshot there). This is a one-time setup for any extension, not "
"just Orcshot's.\n"
"\n"
"Without the extension Orcshot still works — captures use GNOME's screenshot "
"service and there's no tray icon."
msgstr ""

#: src/orcshot/ui/extension_install.py:87
